Relevant columns and their potential usage for the task  

• `objects.object_id`: common key that lets us join `objects` with `vision_api_data`.  
• `objects.period`: the historical period we need to group by.  
• `vision_api_data.object_id`: common key for joining with `objects`.  
• `vision_api_data.labelAnnotations`: ARRAY of STRUCTs generated by the Vision API; each STRUCT has the field `description` that holds a machine‑learning label for the image.  
• `vision_api_data.labelAnnotations.description`: the actual string label we must count.  
• (all other columns are irrelevant for the requested counts but can be selected for inspection/debugging).

Typical conditions that will be useful  

1. `WHERE period IS NOT NULL` – only consider artworks with a period.  
2. `WHERE ARRAY_LENGTH(labelAnnotations) > 0` – skip images with no labels.  
3. `HAVING cnt >= 500` – restrict to labels that appear on ≥ 500 distinct artworks.  
4. Window functions such as `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY period ORDER BY cnt DESC)` to keep the top‑3 labels per period.

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final BigQuery SQL queries (all using the public Met dataset) that build up to the required answer.

```sql
-- 1.  Inspect a handful of periods that exist in the collection
SELECT DISTINCT period
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects`
WHERE period IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Peek at the raw Vision‑API label annotations for a sample object
SELECT object_id, labelAnnotations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data`
WHERE ARRAY_LENGTH(labelAnnotations) > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  List the first 20 (object_id, period) pairs to confirm the join key
SELECT o.object_id, o.period
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
ON o.object_id = v.object_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Extract a flat list of (object_id, label) values
SELECT v.object_id,
       la.description AS label
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v,
UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
WHERE la.description IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Count how many distinct artworks each label is associated with
SELECT la.description AS label,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) AS artworks_labeled
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v,
UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
GROUP BY label
ORDER BY artworks_labeled DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Keep only the labels that appear on 500+ artworks (global filter)
SELECT la.description AS label,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) AS artworks_labeled
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v,
UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
GROUP BY label
HAVING artworks_labeled >= 500
ORDER BY artworks_labeled DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  For each (period, label) pair, count DISTINCT artworks
SELECT o.period,
       la.description AS label,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) AS cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data`  AS v
ON o.object_id = v.object_id,
UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
WHERE o.period IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY o.period, label
HAVING cnt >= 1   -- inspection
ORDER BY cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Apply the ≥ 500‑artworks filter to the aggregated label counts
WITH big_labels AS (
  SELECT la.description AS label
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v,
  UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
  GROUP BY label
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) >= 500
)
SELECT o.period,
       la.description AS label,
       COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) AS cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
ON o.object_id = v.object_id,
UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
JOIN big_labels AS bl
ON la.description = bl.label
WHERE o.period IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY o.period, label
ORDER BY cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Rank labels within each period and keep the top‑3 by count
WITH big_labels AS (
  SELECT la.description AS label
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v,
  UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
  GROUP BY label
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) >= 500
),
period_label_counts AS (
  SELECT o.period,
         la.description AS label,
         COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) AS cnt
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id,
  UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
  JOIN big_labels AS bl
  ON la.description = bl.label
  WHERE o.period IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY o.period, label
)
SELECT period, label, cnt,
       ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY period ORDER BY cnt DESC) AS rn
FROM period_label_counts
ORDER BY period, rn
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10.  FINAL QUERY – Period‑by‑period top‑3 labels, each tied to ≥ 500 artworks
WITH big_labels AS (
  SELECT la.description AS label
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v,
  UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
  GROUP BY label
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) >= 500
),
period_label_counts AS (
  SELECT o.period,
         la.description AS label,
         COUNT(DISTINCT v.object_id) AS cnt
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.the_met.objects` AS o
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.the_met.vision_api_data` AS v
  ON o.object_id = v.object_id,
  UNNEST(v.labelAnnotations) AS la
  JOIN big_labels AS bl
  ON la.description = bl.label
  WHERE o.period IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY o.period, label
),
ranked AS (
  SELECT period, label, cnt,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY period ORDER BY cnt DESC) AS rn
  FROM period_label_counts
)
SELECT period,
       label,
       cnt
FROM ranked
WHERE rn <= 3
ORDER BY period, cnt DESC;
```

Running the final query will return the three most frequent Vision‑API labels for every historical period in The Met collection, provided each label appears on at least 500 different artworks.
